## Test Data Management
- Use factories (`createTestUser()`, `createTestShop()`, etc.) — consistent, reusable
- Clean up after E2E runs — `afterEach` deletes test data by email pattern
- Never use production data — never use real API keys in tests
- MSW handlers for Stripe, Shopify, Anthropic/OpenAI — no real API calls in tests

## CI Integration
Test order in CI (fail fast):
1. `npm run type-check` (fastest — fails first on TS errors)
2. `npm run lint`
3. `vitest --run` (unit + integration)
4. `playwright test` (E2E — slowest, run last)

## Standards
- Descriptive names: "user without active subscription cannot access AI feature" not "test billing"
- One assertion per behavior — multiple assertions per test only when testing a single cohesive outcome
- Tests must break when the feature breaks — if a test never fails, it's not testing anything
- No `any` in test code — same TypeScript strictness as production
- Don't mock what you own — mock external APIs (Stripe, Anthropic), not your own code
